From cc8ea10237bd3933d8538100f5f1ad6988838cdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soulexit <metehan.tanriverdi01@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:26:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 79/84] panvk/jm: less CPU per submit and per draw (ARMSX2),
 WIP

Not CTS-tested yet (dev14).

- One JOB_SUBMIT per vkQueueSubmit (jm-v7 125): the atoms are collected
  per thread and sent together; anything that could wait for one, or
  submits an atom right away, sends them first.
  PANVK_JM_SUBMIT_BATCH=0: one ioctl per atom.
- Non-blocking kbase fd (jm-v7 128): events are read until EAGAIN, without
  a poll(0) before each read; zero-timeout drains do no poll at all.
  PANVK_KBASE_NONBLOCK=0: old behaviour. Waits keep 1 ms poll steps (8 ms
  steps were tried and lost ARMSX2 about 20% of its fps).
- The job history reads the virtual counter instead of clock_gettime(),
  which is a system call on the Galaxy A51's kernel (jm-v7 126).
- Push uniform block reuse by content (jm-v7 127), off by default
  (PANVK_PUSH_REUSE=1): too few hits in ARMSX2 to pay for the checks.
- No relink of an unchanged vertex/geometry/fragment set (jm-v7 129).

NFS Most Wanted (ARMSX2, Galaxy A51): 17-18 fps (a104d4a) -> 16-30 fps by
area; the render thread's driver share 43% -> 39%.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
